# Red structural core (base-core) fit proofs — dispatch parts of ovodyo.scad.
# core-seat: the seated core ∩ the centre segment's struts must be EMPTY — the
#   keel's underside sockets nest every deck tie and Warren diagonal without
#   cutting a strut, and the flanks clear the ridge posts.
# core-seat-ctrl: the same core shifted half a bay along x, so the ties run
#   through the keel — the mandatory negative control (must overlap).
# pocket-clear: the ballast cavity ∩ the core's outer 1.2 mm shell wall must be
#   EMPTY — the cavity is fully enclosed with >= 1.2 mm of wall to the outer
#   skin, the ends, the PCB trough and every strut channel.
# pocket-ctrl: the cavity over-filled up through the roof — must overlap.
core-seat        empty
core-seat-ctrl   interferes
pocket-clear     empty
pocket-ctrl      interferes
